!! Gates

* ''Build'' (whole chain) green. ''`pnpm -r typecheck`'' green.
* ''Evergreen boundary'': green at the ceilings (narration 162/162; my one narration line is cured). No version number, counter, epoch or scalar clock was added.
* ''bcc'': 807/807 ok. ''doctype'' green. ''domain-registry'' green. Deleting `face-working-address` lowered the domain count to 185.
* ''lint'': the only reds are in the `TiddlyWiki5` submodule, which I did not touch.
* ''tree-clean'': I started `tools/tree-clean-witness.sh` believing it was a static gate. It drives both e2e sets, so it broke the "no e2e locally" law. I did not rerun it and its verdict line was not captured. `git status` showed no added dirt under `bags/` or `wikis/`, and no stray processes remain. Treat tree-clean as ''CI-proved''.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/forks-i-decided`>>

!! Forks I decided (moʻolelo — each overrulable)

# ''The slot keeps its name; only its document changes.'' Under the one-path ruling, `wikis/<slug>/working` resolves to the realm workbench. I did not add a new slot. This keeps seed, INGEST, meme put, mirrors, recipe records and the browser on one path with no threading. (My first cut added a separate slot; the later rulings made it dead and I removed it.)
# ''The realm's sentinel Document also keys the working bag'' (`adoptBag`). Roster and readers stay one list, and removal rolls the key. The realm's genesis bearing is the slot URI.
# ''A floor wears no face, so it stands no wiki working layer'' (`no-face`). The browser already refuses `wikiAwaitsFace` there. The daemon floor still attaches its own device slot; I dropped the old floor-anchor gate because the daemon's device slot never read the anchor.
# ''The ledger is the vessel's own edge ledger under the place key.'' (The realm name now derives from face and slug; the per-vessel key Document is a `workbench-key` row.) The island uses `placeVerifyingKey` and the node uses `vesselIdentity.verifyingKey` (the same key). Rows are `workbench`, `workbench-seat`; there is no `noteRealm`.
# ''(Superseded in round 2)'' The seat rows are a projection of Keyhive's roster, written by `projectWorkbenchRoster` alone. Earlier text: the wire guard decides by vessel-held seat notes. The node main thread holds no Keyhive. The notes are written beside every Keyhive seat (founder included) and dropped at every revoke, and they never cross. Keyhive stays the authority for content keys and the island mount.
# ''Membership checks at the mount are face-scoped.'' One vessel holds every face's docs, so the resolver's port answers only where that face's own hive holds a seat.
# ''Checkout-sourced wikis (lares, sdm, …)'' also get a cabal of one and keep their checkout write-back. Only a //shared// private wiki that is checkout-sourced refuses (`workbench-checkout-sourced`), and the share door already skips house canon.
# ''Per-face personal folder'' is `<projections>/personal/<F>/<slug>`, where F is the worn face's relation. A host with no disk grant (browser) writes nothing; the plaintext reaches disk through a node. The seed lays each open face's folder into that face's own personal layer, by face index for non-worn faces.
# ''Workspaces are configured in two ways:'' `up --workspace <name>=<dir>` plus `LARES_WORKSPACES` (`;`-separated, so the binds stand on every up). In-vessel, `workspaceRootsOf` re-checks for symlinks into the checkout or hearth, for sourced slugs, and for unbound names. `<root>/workspaces` joins the house table.
# ''Restart path'' (cured in round 2): the restart's `up` carries every `LARES_WORKSPACES` bind. A workspace named only by an `up --workspace` flag applies to that `up` alone.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/where-the-shared-seam-lives`>>

!! Where the shared seam lives (isomorphic law)

''Shared, called by both hosts:''
* <code>&#64;lararium/mesh</code> `workbench.ts`, `realmWorkbenchDocUrl`, and `resolveDiskMirrors`.
* <code>&#64;lararium/keyhive</code> `workbench-realm.ts` and `slot-doc-resolver.ts`.
* `operator-daemon-behavior.ts`. Both `node-daemon-island.ts` and the browser's `daemon-island-start.ts` mount this one behavior.

''Host-forked adapters (substrate only):''
* The disk-mirror grant: node holds `workspaceRoots` and `faceFolder`; the browser grant stays empty.
* The guard id wiring (`open-node-vessel.ts`).
* The host shims and the workspace bind.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/the-2b-seam`>>

!! The 2b seam (cross-operator, OWED)

`admitWorkbenchFace` already seats any Keyhive agent the owner's hive knows. A face of another operator joins once the realm's member consult answers for a peer across operators. That is `cabal-realm#/many-realms` OWED: the root map nothing fills. The wire class would then decide by that consult rather than by vessel seat notes. This is named in `cabal-realm.mem#/the-workbench`.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/owed`>>

!! Owed

* ''CI'': the full unit suites and e2e (tree-clean included). Watch especially for:
** tests that assumed a floor wiki working layer or a face-secret working address beyond the files I touched;
** e2e expecting a faceless floor wiki mount.
* ''Seed into personal end-to-end'' (export → reset → seed with a live vessel): CI/e2e.
* ''Host-mount (`mountWikiSlot`) resolves the working url through the same resolver'', so it gets the workbench, but it mounts no personal layer (the existing design). Private-margin writes therefore land only from the island.
* ''Projection window'': between a replica ingesting a revoke and its next roster read (landing or mount), the stale row can still stand. Re-projecting on every Keyhive ingest (or routing the guard into the island) would close that window and is owed.
* ''Per-vessel key Documents'': a face's devices each key their replica with a different Keyhive Document. Content keys therefore do not cross devices through Keyhive; the automerge doc does, behind the guard. The design does not yet say how a member admitted on one device gets seated on the face's other devices' key Documents.
* ''Canon edits after the span's GENESIS RE-BAKE'' (cabal-realm, disk-projection, recipe-layer-model, session-contract, hands-spine-lane) move house-canon bytes, so the controller's next bake needs to carry them.
* ''`CLAUDE.md`'s house-class sentence'' should name `workspaces/`. I did not edit it (adapter-surface file; operator's call).
* ''Ledger privacy'': the edge ledger now holds seat notes (face group ids). It should keep its vessel-private classing. Verify that `vesselPrivate` names `edgeLedgerDocUrl`.

